  "limitations": [
    "The use of a rating scale with few steps could potentially compress ratings at the high end of the scale, possibly affecting variance for high preference scenes (p. 4)."
  ],
  "minimum_safe_summary": "This empirical study investigated factors influencing consensus in landscape preference judgments for Swedish farmland grasslands. It found that higher scenic quality was associated with higher consensus (lower variance) in preference judgments. Furthermore, scenes that better matched subjects' mental ideal image of 'pasture' also exhibited lower variance in preference, suggesting that a strong, shared mental representation leads to quicker, more holistic judgments and higher consensus for good examples of that idealized type. No significant effect of group differences was found to explain variability. A limitation noted was the potential for the limited rating scale to compress responses for high-preference scenes.",
